  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhen including `[=/policy container=]` in a bikeshed spec, I get the following error:\n\n```\nMultiple possible 'policy container' dfn refs for '['/']'.\nArbitrarily chose https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#policy-container\nThe following refs show up multiple times in their spec, in a way that Bikeshed can't distinguish between. Either create a manual link, or ask the spec maintainer to add disambiguating attributes (usually a for='' attribute to all of them).\nspec:html; type:dfn; for:/; text:policy container\n  https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#policy-container\n  https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#navigation-params-policy-container\n  https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#link-options-policy-container\n```\n\nI'll put up a patch to add `for=\"...\"` to those latter definitions sometime later today.",
